      <StartPane>
    <Markdown id="bmod_h1_q2_prompt">
## 2. Define your wanted goal behavior

Your wanted goal behavior (WGB) is the behavior you hope to *strengthen*. It
should be the opposite of your unwanted target behavior — if your UTB is not
drinking enough water, your WGB is drinking more water.

Write **one sentence** describing your wanted goal behavior, then **at least
three sentences** explaining why you chose to strengthen it. These reasons
should be the *benefits* of the goal behavior, not the harms of the unwanted
one.
    </Markdown>

    <Markdown id="bmod_h1_q2_recall">
&nbsp;

**{{@bmod_h1_utb_observed.value}}**

&nbsp;
    </Markdown>

    <TextArea id="bmod_h1_q2_response" rows="7"
              placeholder="My wanted goal behavior is..." />

      </StartPane>
      <EndPane>
    <ActionButton id="bmod_h1_q2_btn" label="Check my answer">
